{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492024-have-you-ever-brought-retired-vampire-characters-back-in-the-game","id":1492024,"title":"Have you ever brought retired vampire characters back in the game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-31T12:03:30-07:00","id":1492024,"title":"Have you ever brought retired vampire characters back in the game?","content":"I'm just wondering if you had a stroke of creative game playing and thought having a retired vampire player character brought back would fit the session perfectly?<br /> <br /> I brought this up because of what writer George Miller did with Mad Max Fury Road after going back and forth of bringing his iconic anti-hero back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T17:14:16-07:00","id":1492049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492024-have-you-ever-brought-retired-vampire-characters-back-in-the-game#post1492024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just wondering if you had a stroke of creative game playing and thought having a retired vampire player character brought back would fit the session perfectly?<br /> <br /> I brought this up because of what writer George Miller did with Mad Max Fury Road after going back and forth of bringing his iconic anti-hero back.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As a NPC? Yes, more than a few times, as either mentor, contact and distant or not so distant nemesis even depending on the game, occasion and my narrative needs. Two DA characters of mine have returned as princes in modern era chronicles and others have been everything from harpies to elders, primogen, justicar and at least one anathema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-01-2022, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T03:53:54-07:00","id":1492085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492024-have-you-ever-brought-retired-vampire-characters-back-in-the-game?p=1492049#post1492049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As a NPC? Yes, more than a few times, as either mentor, contact and distant or not so distant nemesis even depending on the game, occasion and my narrative needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this. Characters usually get retired because they become too powerful, so bringing them into a fresh campaign is the equivalent of bringing a level 20 Wizard into a newbie campaign of level 2-4 characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T04:05:01-07:00","id":1492086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492024-have-you-ever-brought-retired-vampire-characters-back-in-the-game?p=1492085#post1492085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically this. Characters usually get retired because they become too powerful, so bringing them into a fresh campaign is the equivalent of bringing a level 20 Wizard into a newbie campaign of level 2-4 characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Usually yes, but depends on one's ST and group i guess. Taking the dust off from a retired character to use him as a PC in whole new stomping grounds in an elder game is also perfectly valid and fair.<br /> <br /> And in fact the only V20 game i ever got the chance to play was a &quot;elders game&quot; where i got to replay Mirkal, my Caitiff methuselah - age-wise, he's &quot;just&quot; 7th gen in potency (what doesn't make him any less dangerous than the 6th or 5th gens of the cabal) - that happens to be an ex- (as in, officially destroyed back in the 80s but not really, what could be problematic for a lot of people including a now Justicar) anathema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-01-2022, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T11:21:11-07:00","id":1492103,"title":"","content":"I've used retried characters a few times as a NPC for a game. My largest problem is that I don't like using player's characters if those players are still in the game because my perception of the character and the player's thoughts could be radically different.<br /> <br /> Normally what I'll do is work through intermediaries to have the retired character still 'active' in the world not directly face to face with the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}